{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared fixtures for the TS\u2194Python scorer parity check. `scoreCard` (bucket-ranking.ts) and",
    "`score_card` (rescore.py) are a deliberate mirror pair with a comment saying so and, until this",
    "file, nothing asserting it. They have already been observed mirroring each other INCLUDING a bug.",
    "",
    "`nowMs` is fixed (2026-08-29T00:00:00Z) so the timeline factor is deterministic on both sides.",
    "",
    "The happy path proves almost nothing. What earns the green is the ASYMMETRIC set below: a card",
    "missing each field a criterion reads, a bucket setting each criterion alone, an unparseable date,",
    "an empty criteria object, the <=3-char word-boundary rule, and the .5 rounding boundary where",
    "The corpus cases were REMOVED with the factor (mig 239) and replaced by the curated record the scorer reads instead: volumes, required items and the admin's highlights, plus the shapes each can arrive in wrong \u2014 a non-array, a null text, whitespace only.",
    "Affinity cases (the learned factor): a liked attribute, a disliked one scoring a real 0, an unjudged one ABSTAINING, a mixed card averaging rather than vetoing, the self-loop guard on a card the customer already judged, and an all-`unreviewed` voter set that must produce no factor at all. The profile is built by each side's SHIPPING builder from `voted`, never read from the fixture \u2014 otherwise the two could agree on a shape the product never produces."
  ],
